/* book exam traps: The alternator generates AC; the diode bridge produces DC. Marks are lost by writing that the alternator generates DC directly. | Output current does not rise forever with speed, and the flat top is not the regulator's doing: the stator reactance grows with speed, so the current self-limits near Imax. The regulator cuts the field only when the loads need less. | Engine rpm is not alternator rpm. With a pulley ratio, Nalt = Nengine × Dengine ÷ Dalt; use the alternator value in f = pN/120. | Cut-in speed is not the same as rated speed. Cut-in is where charging starts; rated speed is where rated current is reached. | For a three-phase full-wave bridge, ripple frequency is 6f, not f. Do not use the single-phase 2f result. */
