/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - An alternator takes mechanical power Pin from the engine belt.
   - P_in is mechanical input power in W; P_out is electrical output power in W; P_cu is total copper loss (stator plus field) in W; P_fe is iron loss in W; P_di is diode loss in W; P_mech is the brush-contact loss P_brush plus bearing and fan l
   - η is efficiency in percent; P_out is useful electrical output power in W; P_in is mechanical input power in W.
   - Use the bus voltage under load for Pout.
   - The regulator holds the bus voltage near a setpoint, about 14 V for a 12 V system.
   - An electromechanical regulator uses a voltage coil and vibrating contacts.
   - D is the field PWM duty cycle, no unit, from 0 to 1; t_on is switch-on time in s; t_off is switch-off time in s.
   - I_f,avg is average field current in A; D is duty cycle; V_bus is bus voltage in V; R_f is field resistance in Ω.
   - The regulator switches the field on and off quickly.
   - Overvoltage protection acts if the regulator or sensing wire fails.
*/
